# Revenew: local SQLite state. Never committed -- these are exactly the two
# files db/schema.sql and db/harness_schema.sql exist to regenerate, and
# committing a real run's data would defeat the harness/runtime isolation the
# whole design rests on (harness.db holds ground truth).
revenew.db
revenew.db-wal
revenew.db-shm
harness.db
harness.db-wal
harness.db-shm
*.db-journal
# Every other SQLite file too -- scratch runs, comparison runs, and the local
# demo_snapshot.db fallback. Databases are build output here: `revenew demo`
# regenerates all of it from the committed cassette, so none of it belongs in
# git. The cassette (cassettes/) is the thing that IS committed, deliberately.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ frontend
# The React console's source lives in frontend/. Its dependencies do not
# belong in git; its BUILD OUTPUT deliberately does.
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/.vite/
frontend/*.local

# Un-ignore the console's own source. `lib/` near the top of this file is a
# stock Python-packaging rule (it means a virtualenv's lib/), and it is
# unanchored, so it also silently swallowed `frontend/src/lib/` -- which
# holds util.js: the hash router, the cached API client, the formatters and
# the playback clock. A fresh clone would have been missing it and the
# console could not build at all, with nothing saying why.
#
# The directory has to be re-included BEFORE its contents: git will not
# re-include a file whose parent directory is still excluded.
!frontend/src/lib/
!frontend/src/lib/**

# revenew/api/static/ is the built console, and it IS committed -- see the
# note in pyproject.toml. The README promises `pip install -e . && revenew
# serve` with no other toolchain, and a judge cloning this repo should not
# need node installed to open the dashboard. This is the same reasoning that
# commits the LLM cassettes rather than requiring an API key.
!revenew/api/static/
DEMO_SCRIPT.md
DESIGN-clickhouse.md 
PLAN.md 
/.claude
